# HarnessFlow on Cursor

This workspace ships HarnessFlow: Matt-aligned main chain (grill → spec → architecture → tickets → implement → ship) plus mechanical gates, progress recovery, auto mode, and pluggable `ext-*` extensions. Skill bodies are adapted from mattpocock/skills (MIT, authorized copy) under `hf-*` names.

## On every development task

1. Load `skills/hf-workflow/SKILL.md` first.
2. Follow the current stage skill: `hf-grill-with-docs` → `hf-to-spec` → `hf-to-architecture` → `hf-to-tickets` → `hf-implement` → `hf-ship`, with `hf-review` (and `hf-code-review` at the code gate) after spec, architecture, and implementation.
3. Before each stage, load matching `skills/ext-*/` by frontmatter binding stage + trigger.

## Hard rules

- Run `skills/hf-workflow/scripts/hf_gate.py check --to <stage>` (or `check --product`) before entering a stage; record RESULT in `progress.md`. FAIL means do not proceed.
- Recover with `skills/hf-workflow/scripts/hf_gate.py status`, not chat memory.
- Underspecification: propose a default, record in `product/assumptions.md`, then proceed.
- Read `CONTEXT.md` / feature `architecture.md` before exploring code; no whole-repo rescan per feature.
- User-perceivable slices need demo acceptance on disk before ship.
- Exploration mode can never ship; close via `conclusion.md` + `check --to close`.
- Author/reviewer separation: reviews in subagent or fresh session; degraded reviews must not self-approve; auto + degraded = hard stop.
- Implement one frontier ticket at a time; build mode uses `hf-tdd` (failing test first).

Pure Q&A or read-only requests need no HarnessFlow.
